.KEY DIR/A,STEP/K,REMOTE/K
.BRA {
.KET }
; Claude install: C:Claude and C:uptelnet. It stands alone: nothing here
; needs UP-Term, and nothing here looks at an UP-Term: assign (that would ask for the volume).
; Run by this archive's Install (an Installer script), which asks the questions:
;   Execute <archive>/Files/install.dos <archive>/Files [STEP <part>]
; From a Shell without Installer the same line installs everything. The Installer
; runs the parts one at a time with STEP (tests/test_dist_addons.py holds the two to
; the same list); the first part, check, has nothing to check for a stand-alone archive.
FailAt 21
; the archive's Files drawer: every name below is relative to it
CD "{DIR}"
; REMOTE "host port": ENVARC:Claude/remote, where Claude Code runs (the NAS); plain
; Claude, with no API key, connects there. Written whenever given (ENVARC: and ENV:).
; The Installer passes it in the variable file ENV:UPTOPTREMOTE (as the base's
; Install does its options: a long path made the command line too long).
Set optremote "{REMOTE}"
If NOT "{STEP}" EQ ""
  If EXISTS ENV:UPTOPTREMOTE
    Set optremote "$UPTOPTREMOTE"
  EndIf
EndIf
If NOT "{STEP}" EQ ""
  Skip {STEP}
EndIf
; @include dist/common/@CHECKFRAG@
Lab claude
; C:Claude, the native Claude client (README): with an API key it is Claude here, with
; ENVARC:Claude/remote it is Claude Code on the NAS through C:uptelnet (this archive's
; copy: the same program as UP-Term.lha's; no ixemul), and with both it asks (CL1).
; An earlier Claude.lha also had C:ClaudeCode (a script) and its icon: they are one app now.
; Its talking to Anthropic needs AmiSSL 5; ENVARC:Claude is where its settings go
; (Install never writes a key).
Copy Claude C:Claude CLONE QUIET
Delete >NIL: C:ClaudeCode QUIET
Copy uptelnet C:uptelnet CLONE QUIET
; C:wasabid (wasabid 0.11b2, MIT, wasabid.LICENSE): uptelnet starts it for the length of one login to the
; NAS, with a key of its own, so Claude Code there can work on this Amiga. It is put in only when no wasabid
; is there (the base kit's, or one of yours): that one stays and is not ours. ENVARC:upkg/Claude/wasabid (in the record drawer) is the
; marker for Uninstall, and a later install updates our own copy.
If NOT EXISTS C:wasabid
  Copy wasabid C:wasabid CLONE QUIET
  MakeDir >NIL: ENVARC:upkg ENVARC:upkg/Claude
  Echo >ENVARC:upkg/Claude/wasabid "installed by Claude.lha"
Else
  If EXISTS ENVARC:upkg/Claude/wasabid
    Copy wasabid C:wasabid CLONE QUIET
  EndIf
EndIf
If NOT EXISTS ENVARC:Claude
  MakeDir ENVARC:Claude
EndIf
If NOT "$optremote" EQ ""
  ; the chosen value always wins (the Installer's page starts with the
  ; existing file's host and port, so a kept answer is the same line)
  If NOT EXISTS ENV:Claude
    MakeDir ENV:Claude
  EndIf
  Echo >ENVARC:Claude/remote "; Claude Code on another computer: host and port. With no API key,"
  Echo >>ENVARC:Claude/remote "; plain Claude connects there (uptelnet). Delete this file to stop."
  Echo >>ENVARC:Claude/remote "$optremote"
  Copy ENVARC:Claude/remote ENV:Claude/remote CLONE QUIET
EndIf
If NOT "{STEP}" EQ ""
  Quit 0
EndIf
Lab launch
; Quick-launch icons: double-click one in UP-Term: to open an UP-Term window running the app
; (IconX opens the XCON: window; it closes when the app ends).
; Stand-alone archive: with no UP-Term: assign there is no UP-Term window and no UP-Term: drawer to
; put them in (XCON: is the UP-Term handler), so nothing is installed and nothing named UP-Term: is touched.
Assign >NIL: UP-Term: EXISTS
If NOT WARN
  Copy "launch/Claude" "launch/Claude.info" UP-Term: CLONE QUIET
  ; the old second icon of Claude.lha 1.0
  Delete >NIL: UP-Term:ClaudeCode UP-Term:ClaudeCode.info QUIET
EndIf
If NOT "{STEP}" EQ ""
  Quit 0
EndIf
; @include dist/common/record.dos
Echo "Claude installed: type  Claude  in a Shell or an UP-Term window, or double-click Claude."
